From 84f98c22ec15e10ed5fec7d1eecc3c549e665f43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taekim <taekim@day34.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 14:48:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 34/36] feat(export): wire 21 new state-C branches into the
 structured JSON exporter
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds fields whose owning record was never constructed anywhere in the
export path before this round (as opposed to S3's field-adds onto
records the exporter already had open):

- SectionDef.footnote_shape/endnote_shape (FootnoteShapeDto)
- Picture.crop/effects.shadow (CropDto/PictureShadowDto, HWPX-only shadow)
- one shared CaptionDto for Table/Picture/DrawingObjAttr/GroupShape/
  ChartShape/OleShape.caption
- OLE and chart shapes, which fell through every catch-all in
  collect_shape_pictures/collect_shape_paths and emitted nothing at
  all — routed to the existing Unsupported tag with new ole/chart
  payloads so Swift's decoder does not need to learn a new block tag
- Document.header (FileHeaderDto) and doc_properties (section_count,
  caret_char_pos)
- DocInfo.bin_data_list (BinDataDeclDto), indexed like borderFills/
  charShapes
- five inline Control variants that fell into build_spans' :
  PageNumberPos, PageHide, NewNumber, Ruby, CharOverlap, plus
  ColumnDef, HiddenComment (needed widening build_spans' signature to
  take &Document so its paragraphs render through build_blocks), Form,
  and every Control::Field (moved from S3, which had classified it
  state B; reaching it usefully needs a new loop over all Field
  controls, not the existing hyperlink filter)
- Paragraph.range_tags/orphan_field_ends (ParaBlock)
- LineShape.connector.control_points (ShapeBlock)
- Table.zones (TableZoneDto)
- BorderFill.diagonal.diagonal_type

All new inline-control markers are zero-width anchor spans (the same
contract Bookmark already uses), so they only ever split an existing
text run at the control's position and add no visible glyphs.

export_s4_c_tier_branches_reach_the_corpus proves 22 of 30 probed keys
arrive with real values across the 340 hwp/hwpx files under samples/
(the other 8 are genuinely rare: ruby, chart, footnote superscript/
inline bits, OLE preview format).
